Z||000006||Master_Sushi||07-09-2001||07:18 PM||||I use a power washer on my fiero(im lazy). My paint isn't perfect but its pretty close to it. I dont get any swirl marks at all. Power washers are good for a light wash, and they are easy/fast to use. So... I was my car every 3-4 days. When it gets really dirty I do have to use a sponge. I also power wax and buff my car every few months   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||prtzlboy||07-09-2001||07:43 PM||||Well I use mits from Malco, and as far as the scratches go, there's no way you can come into physical contact with a car and *not* scratch the paint.  And as said before, the darker the color the more the scratches show.  The best thing to do is wash your car and then use some 3M hand glaze or a similar product to fill in the super fine scratches.  Also, make sure you wash your mit between car washes to get the sand/gravel/dirt etc out of it.||||reg||1
