Z||000010||ChadMan||07-10-2001||08:37 AM||||To dry the car, I use a chamois (real, not synthetic).  I thought that might be the culprit and switched to cotton towels for a while, but nothing changed.<P>I'm glad to hear it's not just me that's experiencing this, and that the color matters so much.  Seemed like my bright red Fieros (84 and 86) never showed these fine scratches, but my 88 sure does (medium red metallic).<P>The worst is my wife's new Saturn.  It is a beautiful cranberry red, and the first time I washed it by hand, I almost cried when I saw those same fine scratches I was getting with the Fiero - and I used a brand-new mitt!  I'm sure they'll buff out, but I wax my cars only 2-3 times a year.<P>Thanks everybody.||||reg||9
Z||000011||starfighter007@msn.com||07-10-2001||04:10 PM||||boy am am I jealous of the finish on your car from the looks of your car ,I would say that probaly on its worst day it still looks better than anything around it I find hard to beleive you only wax her 2 or 3 times a year.sorry I dont have any solutions to your problem.scraches or not you still have fine finish.good luck||||reg||11
